  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombian Human Rights Defenders Visit-parter costs including Father Javier Acosta&apos;s participation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project complements and works closely with the EC funded programme  which works to Improving protection and capacity of human rights defenders and organisations in Colombia. The aim of this partner visit is to:
-  raise awareness of the  of Human Rights situation in Colombia, through lobbying activities in the UK, Brussels and Geneva, in particular focussing on themes of land restitution, protection, mining, peace and victims of the conflict. 
-  hold advocacy meetings at international level to try to improve the state response related to promotion, protection and guarantee of human rights, individual and/or collective freedom and also press work. 
- to support ABColombia in the launching of their report about civil society space.</narrative>
  </description>
